 Cost Estimation in Terraform
Objectives
Install and configure Terraform and Infracost on a bare Ubuntu instance to enable infrastructure cost analysis
Author multi-resource Terraform configurations representing distinct infrastructure tiers and generate per-resource cost breakdowns using Infracost
Produce a structured comparative cost report that quantifies monthly spend differences across infrastructure tiers and identifies the highest-cost resource in each tier
Prerequisites
Comfort navigating and editing files on a Linux command line (creating directories, writing files with a text editor, running shell scripts)
Familiarity with core AWS managed services: EC2, RDS, S3, and Elastic Load Balancing at a conceptual level
Understanding of what Terraform resources and providers are, and how a .tf file is structured
Lab Environment
You will work on a dedicated AWS EC2 Ubuntu instance provided by Al Nafi. The instance has a base Ubuntu installation; you will install all required tools in Task 1.

